{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++ code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cmath>\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing ll = long long;\nconst int MOD = 1000000007;\nconst ll LIM = LLONG_MAX - (ll)MOD * MOD;\n\nint base;\nll n;\n\nusing Matrix = vector<vector<int>>;\n\nMatrix matMul(const Matrix& A, const Matrix& B) {\n    int N = A.size();\n    Matrix C(N, vector<int>(N, 0));\n    for (int i = 0; i < N; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < N; ++j) {\n            ll sum = 0;\n            for (int k = 0; k < N; ++k) {\n                if (sum > LIM) sum %= MOD;\n                sum += (ll)A[i][k] * B[k][j];\n            }\n            C[i][j] = sum % MOD;\n        }\n    }\n    return C;\n}\n\nMatrix identityMatrix(int N) {\n    Matrix I(N, vector<int>(N, 0));\n    for (int i = 0; i < N; ++i) I[i][i] = 1;\n    return I;\n}\n\nvoid run() {\n    cin >> n >> base;\n    int N = base + 1;\n    \n    vector<vector<Matrix>> precomputed(60, vector<Matrix>(base));\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i < base; ++i) {\n        precomputed[0][i] = identityMatrix(N);\n        for (int j = 0; j < N; ++j) {\n            for (int k = 0; k < N; ++k) {\n                if (j == k || i == j) precomputed[0][i][j][k] = 1;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    for (int level = 1; level < 60; ++level) {\n        for (int start = 0; start < base; ++start) {\n            precomputed[level][start] = identityMatrix(N);\n            for (int offset = 0; offset < base; ++offset) {\n                precomputed[level][start] = matMul(precomputed[level][start], precomputed[level-1][(start + offset) % base]);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    Matrix result = identityMatrix(N);\n    int level = 0;\n    ll step = 1;\n    while (step <= n / base) {\n        ++level;\n        step *= base;\n    }\n    \n    int currentBase = 0;\n    for (; level >= 0; --level, step /= base) {\n        int repetitions = (n / step) % base;\n        for (int rep = 0; rep < repetitions; ++rep) {\n            result = matMul(result, precomputed[level][currentBase]);\n            if (++currentBase >= base) currentBase -= base;\n        }\n    }\n    \n    int answer = 0;\n    for (int row = 0; row < N; ++row) {\n        answer = (answer + result[row][base]) % MOD;\n    }\n    cout << answer << '\\n';\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    run();\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\nMOD = 1000000007\nLIM = float('inf')  # Using infinity to simulate LLONG_MAX - MOD * MOD\n\ndef matMul(A, B):\n    N = len(A)\n    C = [[0] * N for _ in range(N)]\n    for i in range(N):\n        for j in range(N):\n            total = 0\n            for k in range(N):\n                if total > LIM:\n                    total %= MOD\n                total += A[i][k] * B[k][j]\n            C[i][j] = total % MOD\n    return C\n\ndef identityMatrix(N):\n    I = [[0] * N for _ in range(N)]\n    for i in range(N):\n        I[i][i] = 1\n    return I\n\ndef run():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    n = int(data[0])\n    base = int(data[1])\n    N = base + 1\n    \n    precomputed = [[None for _ in range(base)] for _ in range(60)]\n    \n    for i in range(base):\n        precomputed[0][i] = identityMatrix(N)\n        for j in range(N):\n            for k in range(N):\n                if j == k or i == j:\n                    precomputed[0][i][j][k] = 1\n    \n    for level in range(1, 60):\n        for start in range(base):\n            precomputed[level][start] = identityMatrix(N)\n            for offset in range(base):\n                precomputed[level][start] = matMul(precomputed[level][start], precomputed[level-1][(start + offset) % base])\n    \n    result = identityMatrix(N)\n    level = 0\n    step = 1\n    while step <= n // base:\n        level += 1\n        step *= base\n    \n    currentBase = 0\n    while level >= 0:\n        repetitions = (n // step) % base\n        for rep in range(repetitions):\n            result = matMul(result, precomputed[level][currentBase])\n            currentBase += 1\n            if currentBase >= base:\n                currentBase -= base\n        level -= 1\n        step //= base\n    \n    answer = 0\n    for row in range(N):\n        answer = (answer + result[row][base]) % MOD\n    print(answer)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    run()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.85\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00017593742813915014, -8.344646857949556e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.06447665393352509, -0.00011383838864276186, -0.2014501690864563, -0.08112450689077377, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.001703955582343042, 0.0, -2.0265558760002023e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -7.152555099310121e-07, -2.50339189733495e-06, -0.01416544709354639, -0.1330653876066208, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.5748875486897305e-05, -0.3041960597038269, -0.00013171759201213717, -3.373566141817719e-05, -0.04307105019688606, -0.00046885941992513835, -2.3841855